  {
    "id": "ba45fb52be692fc9e3c1",
    "source": "The server owner can enter an API key for a public AI model provider (for example, OpenAI, OpenRouter or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) instead of running models on their own hardware. When this is configured, prompts and game content are sent to that provider, and its own privacy policy applies to that data. In the apps, a key you enter for a world on your own device is stored only in that world&apos;s database on the device.",
    "sourceHash": "ba45fb52be692fc9e3c19f5d96e7ab3edd9597bb1d76132e76da59aff9418e2e",
